# The loader's THIRD equality: the named manifest's own declared test against the entry name
# The sweep (gen_fcov.py --validate) checks a manifest's declared test against its FILE STEM; the loader's
# CR-23-L-1 rule checks the stem against the ENTRY NAME. Neither reads the field against the entry, so a manifest
# whose own test field drifted from its stem would load and fail only at run time, unverifiable. This rule closes
# that at load. Defense in depth, not a hole: a mismatch needs both the sweep and the stem rule already satisfied.
# Scope, stated rather than implied: the helper reads ONE field. The manifest's full schema stays the sweep's.
# WHERE THE RED LIVES, and why it is not at the loader: the loader refuses a manifest outside the manifest home
# before it could read the field, so a loader-level fixture would mean writing a bad manifest into a committed
# directory during a self-test. The red is therefore on the helper, with fabricated files in the self-test's own
# temp dir, plus a control on a REAL committed manifest in section 3.
# Taken on a detached archive of 40bd5ef.
